  "seed": "The user dragged a Magnify lens over a screenshot on 2026-10-12 and a stair-stepped grey smear spread across the picture behind it. The lens had been a Pixelate lens switched to Magnify, so it was square cornered with a ring, and a square ring round anything enlarged let the enlarged picture's edge pixels stretch out to the edge of the canvas. The canvas only redraws the area round a moving lens, so each frame of a drag left a patch of that stretch behind. Every check here compares the picture on screen with the same document drawn from scratch, on every move of every drag and after every change, and fails past half a percent. Canvas coordinates are document units.",
